                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "31e99c2c-87e6-40ab-99d7-60b8d3fbe5be",
                                "sense_id": "ae4d9f47-cc46-305e-a78b-c48e36881011",
                                "text": "Previous researchers (for example, Grobbelaar, 2001), have investigated intermine flow."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6758a72-7588-4bdb-92f9-8686fa7aa41b",
                                "sense_id": "ae4d9f47-cc46-305e-a78b-c48e36881011",
                                "text": "In a rather more complex case, the concession offering in Zambia, which has extensive intermine operations in the Copper Belt, allowed bidders to choose to include any combination of Zambia's three railways: mainline operations, intermine operations, and passenger services."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2cb17b0-fbc5-4ae1-b959-ad89dd76d7fe",
                                "sense_id": "ae4d9f47-cc46-305e-a78b-c48e36881011",
                                "text": "Moreover, the concessionaire faced capacity constraints in terms of rolling stock which caused \"deliberate withdrawal from local intermine traffic ”, as the concessionaire \"gave priority to longer-distance traffic from the Copperbelt to South Africa at the expense of local intermine movement of bulk minerals and feeder traffic to Tazara ” ( Bullock 2009: 29, 49, n. 57; also interview Musonda, C)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
